A||||5||88formula||Need help measuring the clutch slave/arm travel. ||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||07-29-2001||08:00 PM||||I need to diagnose my clutch problem once and for all. Nothings sucks more than having to drive a car that won't completely disengage.<P>What I need you guys to do is take a tape measure and measure the travel at the slave cylinder/clutch arm on the transmission and tell me how much yours travels. Right now mine travels 7/8-inch when I hold a tape over the arm and have someone push the clutch pedal to the floor. <P>Also some or one of you guys have e-mailed me and I didn't respond. I didn't respond because the hard drive on my computer died and I lost all my information. My computer is down and I have very limited access.<P>Thanks.    <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||afRaceR||07-29-2001||10:06 PM||||I read somewhere that its supposed to be 1.15 inches at the slave cylinder. I just read this because I'm having problems with my own clutch system.<BR>I can't remember where it was, maybe v8archie's site, I don't know||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||07-29-2001||10:25 PM||||I think you need at least 1 inch.  The ideal travel is 1.2" or so.<P>Does your clutch pedal sit about 1" higher than the brake pedal at rest?  Mine did not with the new steel pedal so I bent the bracket where the M/C pushrod connects to the pedal in a bench vice a little until the pedal was higher than the brake pedal.  This helped me get the travel I wanted and greatly improved the clutch action in my 85 SE (now sold).<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||afRaceR||07-29-2001||10:42 PM||||From what I remember reading, you want1.2" at the master cylinder's piston. which eguates to 1.2" at the slave cylinder's piston but the slave cylinder only moves 1.15". The extra gets bleed off in the master cylinder.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||07-30-2001||05:13 PM||||Can anyone actually measure their travel and tell me what you have.<P>Thanks. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||07-30-2001||07:55 PM||||Anything between 7/8", lowest before clutch failure in a good system an 1 3/16's" with a new clutch.<BR>Also while your measuring watch for the slave to retract with the pedal held to the floor. If this happens you have hydraulic problems.||||reg||1
